# Cloudflare / Netlify _headers — security headers (plan §7).
# Target: A+ on securityheaders.com and Mozilla Observatory.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy's script-src/style-src (with per-build hashes for
# inline scripts/styles) is emitted by Astro as a <meta> tag — see the `csp`
# block in astro.config.mjs, so it needs no maintenance here. This file adds the
# directives a <meta> CSP cannot express (frame-ancestors) plus the other
# security headers. (scripts/csp-hash.mjs remains if you ever move CSP fully to
# headers instead of meta.)

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
